      "writtenOn": "2026-11-23T20:54:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "After scanning an open interpolated string brace like `s!\"hi {`, inInterpString is cleared and brace stays 0 while interpBraceTop is 1, so both hasOpenLiteralOrComment() and hasOpenDelimiters() return false. Every hasOpenLiteralOrComment caller in the stack already ORs in hasOpenInterpBrace(), while LeanParser (change 658564) calls hasOpenDelimiters(lexState) without checking hasOpenInterpBrace(), allowing a `where` inside a multi-line `s!\"...{\\n ... where ...\\n}\"` to enter inWhereBlock prematurely. Include interpBraceTop \u003e 0 in both predicates (and update LeanLexerTest.java:293-294).",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 343,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 353,
        "endChar": 9999
