      "writtenOn": "2026-11-23T20:54:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "hasIdentPartBefore returns true on the first isIdentStart code point encountered while scanning backward, so it still misclassifies scientific/radix/underscore numbers (1e3, 0x1, 0xff, 0b1, 0o7, 1_000) and char literals (\u0027a\u0027) as identifier prefixes. That breaks public matchRawStringOpen(\"1e3r#\\\"\\\"\\\"#\", 3), matchCharLiteral(\"0x1\u0027\\\"\u0027\", 3), matchNumberLiteral(\"\u0027a\u0027123\", 3), and downstream sequential callers in LeanParser and LeanHighlighter. Walk back to the start of the contiguous isIdentPart run and scan forward over leading number or char literals to check if the token ending at i is an identifier, and consider making matchCharLiteralAt/matchRawStringOpenAt/matchNumberLiteralAt package-private so LeanParser and LeanHighlighter can avoid lookback altogether.",
