      "writtenOn": "2026-11-23T20:54:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Entering `{` from inInterpString (lines 791-805 and 1299-1305) does not save or reset state.interpCmd, and `{` / `}` while interpBraceTop \u003e 0 unconditionally reset it to INITIAL (here and at lines 1360-1385). That breaks both braced terms inside interpolations (like `s!\"{throwErrorAt { a :\u003d 1 } \"{\u0027\\\"\u0027}\"}\"`) and interpolated strings inside command refs (like `throwErrorAt (← mkRef s!\"{x}\") \"bad {sorry}\"`), flipping quote parity and hiding sorry in hygiene mode. Save and reset interpCmd on a parallel stack when entering `{` from inInterpString, forward inner `{` and non-closing `}` (nextDepth \u003e 0) to advanceInterpCmdOnPunct, and restore the saved state when returning to inInterpString.",
