      "writtenOn": "2026-11-23T19:28:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "When `maskOutput` is true and `startCp` is a non-identifier supplementary Unicode code point (`startLen \u003d\u003d 2`, e.g., an emoji or supplementary math symbol inside `dbg_trace \"{😀}\"`), this appends only one space while advancing `i` by `startLen`, shrinking the output and breaking the 1:1 UTF-16 offset invariant. Please use `appendSpaces(out, startLen)` instead of `out.append(\u0027 \u0027)` when `ch !\u003d \u0027\\n\u0027`.",
