      "message": "advanceLeanLexStateCore only calls state.advanceInterpCmdOnNewline() on line comments (line 1347), never at normal end-of-line. Because advanceLeanLexState, hasUnterminatedLiteralOrComment, findMultiLineAttributeEnd, and LeanParser split on newlines before calling this method, multi-line forms like `throwNamedErrorAt stx\\nmyErr \"{\u0027\\\"\u0027}\"` or `trace[a\\n] \"{\"` diverge from stripLeanCommentsAndStrings and corrupt quote parity. Call advanceInterpCmdOnNewline() before returning -1 whenever outside a comment or literal body (and also add INTERP_EXPECT_TRACE_OPEN to InterpCmdState.onNewline(), or have onNewline() delegate to onPunct(\u0027\\n\u0027), so it matches line 216).",
